      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-6,4],$ find $\\text{E}[X].$",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-6$ and $b=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{-6+4}{2}=-1.\n$$",
